    }
   ],
   "addLines": [
    {
     "month": "2026-10",
     "line": {
      "id": "sam-laptop-10",
      "date": "2026-10-02",
      "amount": 120000,
      "role": "spending",
      "seriesId": "laptop-plan",
      "name": "Laptop"
     }
    },
    {
     "month": "2026-10",
     "line": {
      "id": "sam-refund-10",
      "date": "2026-10-03",
      "amount": 120000,
      "role": "other_in",
      "name": "Laptop refund"
     }
    }
   ],
   "purchase": {
    "price": 5000,
    "taxPercent": null,
    "oneOffFees": 0,
    "itemType": "general",
    "purpose": null,
    "emergency": false,
    "envelopeId": null,
    "categoryId": null,
    "pay": {
     "mode": "once"
    },
    "extras": {},
    "share": "personal",
    "foreign": null
   },
   "expect": {
    "code": "fits_month",
    "legacyState": "fits",
    "band": 2,
    "split": [
     {
      "source": "month",
      "amount": 5000
     }
    ],
    "unspentAfter": 235000,
    "month": {
     "moneyIn": 400000,
     "moneyOut": 357500,
     "monthLeft": 42500
    },
    "working": "Sam bought a 120,000 laptop on 2026-10-02 on a plan, cancelled on return (series ended 2026-10-03). The unspent anchor of 2026-10-02 was 120,000 (after the purchase). The 120,000 refund (other_in, no countsAs, so not income) lands 2026-10-03, after the anchor, so unspent is 120,000+120,000 = 240,000, the pre-purchase figure. breakdown.other nets the returned purchase out of the month: moneyOut stays 150,000+30,000+10,000+137,500+30,000 = 357,500, moneyIn 400,000, monthLeft 42,500. A 5,000 check <= 42,500 -> fits_month; the plan pins unspentAfter = 240,000 (the pre-purchase figure). Band 2 (5,000 is not < 5,000). CORRECTION (05.1-25): the rolled unspent (funds.unspent.value) is 240,000, the pre-purchase figure, and the golden pins that separately. The unspent_before_after fact is for the 5,000 check being asked now: 240,000-5,000 = 235,000 (the same subtraction as situation 02), so unspentAfter is 235,000, not 240,000."
   },
   "source": "D-18"
  },
